So how deep something is.

189
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:25,120
Something is shallow, it's not very deep.

190
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,940
So there's very little water.

191
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:34,980
But if there's a lot of water, maybe if you swim and you can't touch your feet on the ground, we call that deep.

192
00:09:34,980 --> 00:09:39,260
So shallow is very low water and deep is lots and lots of water.

193
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:40,240
Okay, very good.

194
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:42,420
So you'll usually find this in the ocean.

195
00:09:42,740 --> 00:09:47,060
If you go further, further, further in, it'll get deeper and deeper and deeper.

196
00:09:47,060 --> 00:09:47,780
And more and more dangerous.

197
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:49,480
Right.

198
00:09:49,480 --> 00:09:55,640
And this is why the mom also told the kid to not pass that sandbar that was ahead.

199
00:09:56,260 --> 00:09:57,220
Okay, sandbar.

200
00:09:57,440 --> 00:10:03,260
This is a piece of sand that basically rises very high in the water.

201
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:10,660
So usually when you're on the beach and you go into the water and it gets deeper and deeper and then all of a sudden it gets high again and there's more sand.

202
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:16,320
And so that part that you can stand on, that sand out in the water, that's called a sandbar.

203
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,100
It's almost like a little island.

204
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:18,100
Yeah, exactly.

205
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:23,800
And as you said, usually it gets deeper, deeper, then you have the sandbar so it gets higher.

206
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:27,440
But usually if you pass the sandbar, it's going to get really deep all of a sudden.

207
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:27,580
That's right.

208
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:32,240
So that's why the mother doesn't want her child to go past the sandbar.

209
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:33,240
Right.

210
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:42,860
And as well, if you're ever swimming in a swimming pool in the ocean, it's always a good idea if you don't know how to swim well or if you have children to take along little floaties.

211
00:10:43,140 --> 00:10:43,880
Okay, floaties.

212
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:45,880
I like this word.

213
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:54,440
Floaties are plastic rings that you put around your arms or maybe around your stomach and they're filled with air.

214
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:55,640
Right.

215
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:57,720
So when you go in the water, they help you float.

216
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:57,930
Exactly.

217
00:10:58,720 --> 00:11:03,030
So this is a very common thing to put on children because they don't know how to swim well.

218
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:09,520
So you put them little floaties on their arms or around their stomachs and then they can just float and they won't drown.

219
